 "notes": "Headline 95% CL upper limit on g_agamma (red Sgr A* curve) from Fig. 1 (combined three EHT sub-array data sets, polarization_v1.pdf in the e-print), extracted as vector paths and calibrated to the log-log axes. Curve spans m_a ~ 1e-20 to 1e-17 eV; strongest bound ~7e-13 GeV^-1 near 3e-19 eV. Birefringence search using position-angle oscillation of polarized mm emission from Sgr A*. Jagged features/upward jumps are physical (degeneracy with background phase at low mass, non-significant favored regions at high mass) as described in the text. DM density is not the local 0.4 GeV/cm^3: the limit uses a solitonic-core+NFW profile (Eq. 2.12) for ALP DM near the SMBH; the position-angle parameterization (Eq. 2.9) is normalized to rho_DM = 2e9 GeV/cm^3, the value recorded here, but the actual assumed density at the source is mass-dependent via Eq. 2.12. Delta-chi2 = 2.7 threshold.",
